<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

    <!--
      Accepted OWASP Dependency-Check exclusions.

      Empty on purpose. Nothing has been suppressed, and nothing should be suppressed without a
      note here saying which CVE, which dependency, and why it does not apply — "the build was
      red" is not a reason. The scan is informational in CI (see build.gradle for why), so there
      is never any pressure to silence a finding just to get a green tick.

      The shape of an entry, for whoever needs the first one:

      <suppress>
          <notes>CVE-XXXX-NNNNN affects the servlet path of this library. ParcelFlow uses it only
                 for <specific thing>, which does not reach that code. Reassess on the next
                 Spring Boot upgrade.</notes>
          <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/group/artifact@.*$</packageUrl>
          <cve>CVE-XXXX-NNNNN</cve>
      </suppress>
    -->

</suppressions>
